    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-13,\\ p=3,\\ q=1,\\ r=-3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2x-5)(px^2+qx+r)&=2px^3+(2q-5p)x^2+(2r-5q)x-5r\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the coefficients of $x^3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2p&=6\\\\p&=3\\end{align*}$$\nEquating constant terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5r&=15\\\\r&=-3\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the coefficients of $x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2r-5q&=-11\\\\-6-5q&=-11\\\\q&=1\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the coefficients of $x^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=2q-5p\\\\&=2(1)-5(3)\\\\&=-13\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
